[
    {
        "championName": "Alistar",
        "difficulty": "Minor",
        "idmatchup": 1,
        "tips": "Very strong engage support right now, but you can E him away as he goes in for his combo. You should always take E level 1 against him so you're safe in case he gets the level two powerspike first.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Ashe",
        "difficulty": "Minor",
        "idmatchup": 2,
        "tips": "Ashe can be very annoying in lane, but if you're able to hit a hook on her she'll be in mayor trouble. She doesn't scale very well either as she only really has her ult lategame. Consider getting Mikael's Crucible vs her.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Bard",
        "difficulty": "Minor",
        "idmatchup": 3,
        "tips": "In lane he's not going to be a problem, but he should be able to outroam you as he's faster than you. Try to mitigate this by making a play on his adc or being where he's going before the play happens.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Blitzcrank",
        "difficulty": "Even",
        "idmatchup": 4,
        "tips": "Skill matchup (between the adcs to not get hooked). Be aware that he can hook people out of your lantern if he times it right.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Brand",
        "difficulty": "Major",
        "idmatchup": 5,
        "tips": "Stay away from minions as he will use E to hit you and your adc for free poke. If he misses his stun you have a window to go in and punish.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Braum",
        "difficulty": "Minor",
        "idmatchup": 6,
        "tips": "Braum has the power to make lanes very boring or very explosive, this mostly depends on the adc he is paired up with. Try to punish him for wasting his E on poke.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Hwei",
        "difficulty": "Minor",
        "idmatchup": 7,
        "tips": "Against Hwei, you need to focus on not standing too close to minions because of his QQ aoe and punish him if he ever misses or wastes any of his E spells.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Janna",
        "difficulty": "Even",
        "idmatchup": 8,
        "tips": "Janna scales stronger than you (like most enchanters), and has amazing disengage tools. Try to not stand next to your adc as she might hit you both with Q and don't stand too still when you see that she starts using her Q.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Karma",
        "difficulty": "Even",
        "idmatchup": 9,
        "tips": "Don't stand to close to minions as her Q is a small aoe (larger with mantra). You can look for fights after she has used her R as it is a large part of her early game power (She has ult level one, you don't)",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Leona",
        "difficulty": "Even",
        "idmatchup": 10,
        "tips": "Really strong engage support, you can deny her engage by flaying her away when she casts E. You should always take E level 1 against her so you're safe in case she gets the level two powerspike first.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Lulu",
        "difficulty": "Minor",
        "idmatchup": 11,
        "tips": "Don't underestimate Lulus damage, especially not if she is maxing E first. As most enchanter supports you need to make stuff happen early game.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Lux",
        "difficulty": "Major",
        "idmatchup": 12,
        "tips": "Lux is really strong and will make sure you know it if you give her the space. Don't get hit by her spells and try to punish her if she misses her Q.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Maokai",
        "difficulty": "Major",
        "idmatchup": 13,
        "tips": "Maokai is really overtuned as of late and will be really effective at roaming or killing your adc in lane. It's quite difficult to peel him off because of his W making him untargetable.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Milio",
        "difficulty": "Tiny",
        "idmatchup": 14,
        "tips": "You win early against just about any lane with Milio. His level 1 is quite strong because of his two charges of his shield, but you can still punish him early game. He can knock you away with his Q while you're traveling with Q.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Morgana",
        "difficulty": "Major",
        "idmatchup": 15,
        "tips": "Black shield does not allow any fun... Look for fights if she wastes her E in lane. Would be a much bigger threat if she was actually a viable support.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Nami",
        "difficulty": "Major",
        "idmatchup": 16,
        "tips": "Do not underestimate Namis damage, punish her if she misses her Q, but don't over commit, her lane partner might chase you down with the slows from Nami.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Nautilus",
        "difficulty": "Major",
        "idmatchup": 17,
        "tips": "His hook is faster than yours so he can hook you reactively. Care for his kill pressure so don't roam for too long.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
    {
        "championName": "Pyke",
        "difficulty": "Extreme",
        "idmatchup": 18,
        "tips": "Pyke is very slippery and will also roam faster than you. Try to punish the enemy adc when he leaves and be aware that he has the tools to do the same to your adc if you leave for too long.",
        "tipsFr": null
    },
